# SourceBD Lean Context Boot

Read these once per session, in this order, and never again in the session:

1. `AGENTS.md`
2. `context/agent-brief.md`
3. `context/current-state.md` (cap 16 KB)
4. `context/feature-specs/active.md` (cap 6 KB)

Then only the task-relevant source of truth named in `AGENTS.md` rule 3.

`context/archive/*` and inactive `context/feature-specs/*` are never read
whole: grep for the heading, read that section. Same for any file over
~10 KB you did not write this session.

Do not re-read a boot file after editing it. Do not edit `AGENTS.md` or
`agent-brief.md` mid-session.

For small edits, read the affected code and narrow context sections only.
